silm:instances_papers_11_base_commutative_diagram_chapters_26_circuit_imprint_tensor_sections_01_three_axes_unpacked_concrete_anchor_0#substrateaxis_physical silm:hasLongDescription "The SubstrateAxis_physical is the physical pole of the substrate axis: a microchip-tagged cat (Mittens, microchip 985112345678901), a granite chunk, a signed vet record -- all PHYSICAL substrates. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'SubstrateAxis_physical', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
